## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | js/common/developmentModeAdaptive.js | ⚠️ important removestaleappendix never detects a failed delete — dmtools file delete signals failure via the return object not by throwing verified empirically against the installed dmtools runtime probe script via dmtools run json nonexistent deleted false real deleted true file delete never throws — it returns deleted false for a missing path and deleted true on success this code and the test at test developmentmodeadaptive js 565 which simulates failure by throwing assume the opposite contract so the catch below is dead code and the documented one honest warning on a deletion failure js common developmentmodeadaptive js 388 390 can never fire javascript try remove path developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path catch e console warn could not remove the stale plan mode appendix at e why it matters on a reused workspace where a previous leg materialized the appendix a routed to default adaptive leg relies entirely on this cleanup the condition script isdevelopmentmodeplan js then probes the file — a surviving stale file means the plan protocol appendix rides a routed default prompt that directly violates this pr s own invariant docs development mode md §2 3 a routed to default leg and any shadow leg remove stale appendix state so their prompts stay byte identical to default and ac4 shadow legs are safe the condition script s zero read guard is the second line of defense there but routed default legs have no backstop suggested fix — consult the return object and only warn when a file actually existed a plain deleted false is the normal clean workspace response and must stay quiet javascript function removestaleappendix io var remove io io file delete file delete var existed typeof read path developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path string var result null try result remove path developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path catch e result null defensive only — the platform does not throw if existed result result deleted true console warn could not remove the stale plan mode appendix at developmentmodeplan plan appendix file path result and update fsrecorder s failure test test developmentmodeadaptive js 565 to simulate the real failure shape file delete returning deleted false after an existence probe instead of a throw |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 6b9c381a460c972b02364b057e77f35cf3f0cec4
Current head: 3881e5ec6b4e492a5a1ec9b8ffe2e529d0386804

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

